From cf20e9eeba41cd94f0dbf8010aeb5a45e3af1429 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 02:28:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] strings and comments: the help of Low-Latency in es_ar and
 es_mx, a release name
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The help of "Dolby Vision Low-Latency" (#31921) was rewritten in en_gb
and es_es when Low-Latency could also be sent where the TV takes
Standard; es_ar and es_mx kept the text of before, which says the
opposite of the setting now. Both now have the English text and the
Spanish of es_es, with "video" for "vídeo" as their other strings have
it.

A comment named a release by its number alone: it says "1.0 RC4" now.
---
 .../skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po  | 4 ++--
 .../skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po  | 4 ++--
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp                   | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po b/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po
index 04acf4b..db28858 100644
--- a/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po
+++ b/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po
@@ -2185,8 +2185,8 @@ msgstr "Dolby Vision Low-Latency (mapeado por el reproductor)"
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
 #. Hades: help of setting "videoscreen.hadesdvlowlatency" (core #39871)
 msgctxt "#31921"
-msgid "On a TV input that offers Dolby Vision only as Low-Latency (its game mode, or a TV that has no other), sends Dolby Vision that way: LibreELEC Hades maps the picture to the display itself, as a player does for Low-Latency, with the BT.2390 curve guided by the level 1 metadata of each scene, to the peak and the colours that the display gives for it. The mapping is that of LibreELEC Hades, not that of Dolby. A display that takes Dolby Vision Standard keeps it, whatever this says. Applies from the next video."
-msgstr "En una entrada de la TV que solo ofrece Dolby Vision como Low-Latency (su modo de juego, o una TV que no tiene otro), envía así Dolby Vision: LibreELEC Hades mapea la imagen a la pantalla él mismo, como hace un reproductor en Low-Latency, con la curva BT.2390 guiada por los metadatos de nivel 1 de cada escena, al pico y a los colores que la pantalla da para ello. El mapeo es el de LibreELEC Hades, no el de Dolby. Una pantalla que acepta Dolby Vision Standard lo conserva, diga lo que diga este ajuste. Se aplica desde el siguiente video."
+msgid "On a TV input that offers Dolby Vision only as Low-Latency (its game mode, or a TV that has no other), sends Dolby Vision that way: LibreELEC Hades maps the picture to the display itself, as a player does for Low-Latency, with the BT.2390 curve guided by the level 1 metadata of each scene, to the peak and the colours that the display gives for it. The mapping is that of LibreELEC Hades, not that of Dolby. A display that takes Dolby Vision Standard keeps it, unless \"Low-Latency also where the TV takes Standard\" is on. Applies from the next video."
+msgstr "En una entrada de la TV que solo ofrece Dolby Vision como Low-Latency (su modo de juego, o una TV que no tiene otro), envía así Dolby Vision: LibreELEC Hades mapea la imagen a la pantalla él mismo, como hace un reproductor en Low-Latency, con la curva BT.2390 guiada por los metadatos de nivel 1 de cada escena, al pico y a los colores que la pantalla da para ello. El mapeo es el de LibreELEC Hades, no el de Dolby. Una pantalla que acepta Dolby Vision Standard lo conserva, salvo que \"Low-Latency también donde la TV acepta Standard\" esté activado. Se aplica desde el siguiente video."
 
 #: xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
 #. Hades: notification for a Dolby Vision video on a display that offers Low-Latency only, where the output driver can send it; one sentence, the details are in the log (core #39872)
diff --git a/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po b/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po
index f140ce5..1f0913e 100644
--- a/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po
+++ b/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po
@@ -2205,8 +2205,8 @@ msgstr "Dolby Vision Low-Latency (mapeado por el reproductor)"
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
 #. Hades: help of setting "videoscreen.hadesdvlowlatency" (core #39871)
 msgctxt "#31921"
-msgid "On a TV input that offers Dolby Vision only as Low-Latency (its game mode, or a TV that has no other), sends Dolby Vision that way: LibreELEC Hades maps the picture to the display itself, as a player does for Low-Latency, with the BT.2390 curve guided by the level 1 metadata of each scene, to the peak and the colours that the display gives for it. The mapping is that of LibreELEC Hades, not that of Dolby. A display that takes Dolby Vision Standard keeps it, whatever this says. Applies from the next video."
-msgstr "En una entrada de la TV que solo ofrece Dolby Vision como Low-Latency (su modo de juego, o una TV que no tiene otro), envía así Dolby Vision: LibreELEC Hades mapea la imagen a la pantalla él mismo, como hace un reproductor en Low-Latency, con la curva BT.2390 guiada por los metadatos de nivel 1 de cada escena, al pico y a los colores que la pantalla da para ello. El mapeo es el de LibreELEC Hades, no el de Dolby. Una pantalla que acepta Dolby Vision Standard lo conserva, diga lo que diga este ajuste. Se aplica desde el siguiente video."
+msgid "On a TV input that offers Dolby Vision only as Low-Latency (its game mode, or a TV that has no other), sends Dolby Vision that way: LibreELEC Hades maps the picture to the display itself, as a player does for Low-Latency, with the BT.2390 curve guided by the level 1 metadata of each scene, to the peak and the colours that the display gives for it. The mapping is that of LibreELEC Hades, not that of Dolby. A display that takes Dolby Vision Standard keeps it, unless \"Low-Latency also where the TV takes Standard\" is on. Applies from the next video."
+msgstr "En una entrada de la TV que solo ofrece Dolby Vision como Low-Latency (su modo de juego, o una TV que no tiene otro), envía así Dolby Vision: LibreELEC Hades mapea la imagen a la pantalla él mismo, como hace un reproductor en Low-Latency, con la curva BT.2390 guiada por los metadatos de nivel 1 de cada escena, al pico y a los colores que la pantalla da para ello. El mapeo es el de LibreELEC Hades, no el de Dolby. Una pantalla que acepta Dolby Vision Standard lo conserva, salvo que \"Low-Latency también donde la TV acepta Standard\" esté activado. Se aplica desde el siguiente video."
 
 #: xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
 #. Hades: notification for a Dolby Vision video on a display that offers Low-Latency only, where the output driver can send it; one sentence, the details are in the log (core #39872)
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp
index 36deceb..5705612 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp
@@ -1054,7 +1054,7 @@ CVideoPlayerVideo::EOutputState CVideoPlayerVideo::OutputPicture(const VideoPict
 
     // Hades: a wait that was called off (a flush or the stream closing set m_bAbortOutput) is no
     // timeout: only a real one is a warning (idea of CroqueMr's build; seen after every stop in
-    // the logs of 1.0 RC3 and RC4). What follows is as before.
+    // the logs of 1.0 RC3 and 1.0 RC4). What follows is as before.
     if (m_bAbortOutput)
       CLog::Log(LOGDEBUG, "{} - the wait for a buffer was called off", __FUNCTION__);
     else if (m_speed != DVD_PLAYSPEED_PAUSE)
-- 
2.53.0

